# Build-context denylist for the Python health-endpoint tier (port 8000).
#
# The sibling Dockerfile copies its runtime files by name, so this file does not
# decide what lands in the image -- it decides what the daemon has to receive before
# the build starts. Kept an explicit denylist rather than a `*` with `!`
# re-inclusions, where one mis-ordered negation drops a file silently.
#
# Never exclude pyproject.toml or config/health.json: health.py falls back to
# compiled-in literals carrying the same strings, so an image built without them
# serves a byte-identical body and no reading of /health can tell the two apart --
# only an existence check inside the image, or the "health configuration degraded"
# line server.py prints at start-up. So no broad *.py, *.toml, *.json, config or
# .python-version pattern.

# Version-control metadata. Here .git is a one-line gitdir POINTER file, because this
# tier is consumed as a submodule, but it names a path inside the superproject's
# object store and local remote-tracking configuration must never enter a layer.
.git
.gitmodules
.gitignore

# Python execution residue from a local run: machine-specific, and pure
# build-context weight. The Dockerfile copies named .py files and config/ only, so
# these could not reach the image in any case. The plain and `**/` forms are both
# listed because a leading segment without `**` matches at the context root only.
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
**/*.pyc

# Local environment files; .env.example is the tracked documentation template and is
# named explicitly for the reader.
.env
.env.example
.env.*

# Documentation. Read from the repository, not from inside a container.
README.md

# Build-time-only inputs, read from the context before the build.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# A .github directory, whenever one is added: read from the repository, never from
# inside an image.
.github

# Test sources. A runtime image ships neither the tests nor the servers they start on
# ephemeral ports.
test_app.py

# The nested Java tier. It is a first-class part of this project and a TRACKED
# gitlink -- it must never appear in .gitignore -- but it builds its own image from
# its own Dockerfile and serves its own endpoint on port 8080.
nested_child_repo_10_LOC
